codex
A better invariant shape is available: iterate directly over `b` while carrying the current rotation. The reference iterator then exposes one constructor of the remaining character sequence per iteration, so K can perform structural circular reasoning without unboundedly expanding an integer-indexed oracle. I’m switching to that equivalent iterative implementation.
